      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_11",
      "quote": "Peer-­ reviewed studies were considered eligible if they included at least 100 people with laboratory confirmed and/or clinically diagnosed COVID-­ 19. Without a clear, internationally agreed case definition, we included studies that reported symptoms or outcomes assessed at 12 or more weeks post COVID-­ 19 onset.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies the population (people with COVID-19), study design (implied by the inclusion of peer-reviewed studies and exclusion of preprints), and follow-up requirements (12 or more weeks post onset)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_12",
      "quote": "There were no language restrictions. Reviews and opinion pieces were excluded. Studies were excluded if they included fewer than 100 participants, to avoid small study effects, 18 or the follow-­ up was unclear or less than 12 weeks post onset.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies language restrictions (none), publication status (peer-reviewed only, as noted in text_11 and text_14), and search dates (text_10)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The manuscript does not explicitly state whether studies were excluded because outcomes were not measured versus because results were not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_12",
      "quote": "We presented symptom proportions by different settings, as presented in the individual studies: hospitalised, non-­ hospitalised or a mix of both populations if no subset data were available. Symptoms were broadly grouped into physiological clusters through discussion with clinicians. ... Additional subgroup analysis was conducted to explore the modification of the following factors on proportion of symptoms: hospitalisation, settings, continents and follow-­ up timing.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies how studies were grouped for synthesis (by setting: hospitalised, non-hospitalised, or mixed) and mentions subgroup analyses."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_12",
      "quote": "Studies were excluded if they included fewer than 100 participants, to avoid small study effects",
      "reason": "A rationale is provided for the restriction on study size (to avoid small study effects)."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 100
